Iranian students are prepared to die for their country's nuclear program.
They formed a human shield.
Hundreds of university students formed human shields around nuclear facilities in Iran.
With their gesture they want to express their support for their country's nuclear program in the face of a possible Israeli attack.
The students prayed Tuesday at noon before the facilities and then chanted death slogans to the U.S. and Israel.
Hundreds of university students formed on Tuesday in the Iranian city of Isfahan human shields around the nuclear technology center where uranium is being worked.
They intend to show that they are ready to defend their country's nuclear program with their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), in a recent report, found that Iran, according to all indications, is eager to obtain nuclear weapons.
In Israel there is talk of a possible attack on Iran's nuclear facilities.
The students prayed at no-nothing at the Isfahan nuclear facility and then threw death slogans at the U.S. and Israel.
In the event of an attack, aimed at paralyzing the Iranian nuclear programme, according to Israeli sources it would be achieved not only the Isfahan power plant, but also Natanz &apos; s facilities, where uranium enriched.
An obese kid's diary menu: don't have breakfast and dinner sausages
More than a third of children between the ages of 9 and 13 have overheating problems, where overweight affects 9 per cent of the school population and obesity at 5 per cent.
Obese children come mostly from families with an unhealthy lifestyle, according to current research.
Redemonstrates is the importance of the environment where it grows to a healthy development of the person, as well as the models that serve as a reference.
At the table, obsessed children feed, for example, on sausages at least twice as often as children from families with normal weight.
For dinner, more than 19 per cent of obese had dined chips the day before testing, which is linked to the "obcess obesity isn't a coincidence."
There's no habit of sports in the families of over-threnched children, which is applicable to the majority of today's families, where only 15 per cent of the children replied that their parents, at least once a week, find time for physical exercise.
A survey of 900 children
The survey was carried out at the end of the last school year and almost 900 children of basic education from all over the world participated.
Already it was the second edition of the "Oessian obesity is not a coincidence," supported by the General Health Insurance Company and Unilever.
Until now, more than 12,000 children have participated in the project from the 4th to the 8th year.
Pretty dietary and a lot of exercise in the family are determinants, which significantly reduce the number of children who are overhea and even obesity.
"Only half of the children surveyed have replied that they have five meals a day according to the diet: breakfast, lunch, food, snack and dinner, which is one of the basic conditions for a healthy diet," says one of the results of the survey.
Without breakfast but bounty for dinner
The specialists warn that, in a healthy development, it is also important the details, which also count, such as having a fixed hour for breakfast in the family.
However, only 23 per cent of school children's families have breakfast at the same time.
In the majority of the families, each breakfast alone.
But the worst thing was to discover that 10 per cent of households don't have break-eaten.
Breakfast, however, is the basis of a correct daily diet.
The study shows that unhealthy chips are consumed much more frequently by families of obese children.
Almost everyone - regardless of the weight - drink sweet refreshments (70 per cent) every day.
More than 40 per 40 per cent of children surveyed usually do sport, but among their parents this result is reduced to less than half, only 15 per cent.
Fashicate your diet
The next phase of the study made it possible for the chosen boys (204 boys and 172 girls of 13 schools) to create their own diets from all possible offers according to their tastes and opinions.
"The food preferences of Czech children between the ages of 12 and 15, from the point of view of a healthy eating, are very distant from the ideal."
His favorite foods include pasta, meat and candy
"It's mostly alarming the popularity of candy refreshers," warns the final report of the study.
As a main meal, the pasta takes the pasta and is closely followed by bird's flesh.
Practically, children always reject legume and taste for fish and veg is very low.
Change to healthy habits
At the same time, the study shows that children are willing to change their eating habits if they receive fair information.
"In the control group of the participants in the study, who completed the questionnaire after finishing the prevention program "obesity isn't a coincidence," in many cases there was an important change in favor of the principles of healthy eating," the results of the study indicate.
It attracts attention, for example, when it comes to sweet sodas, where many children would start preferring normal and running water.
Kids would also more frequently choose bird meat and fish for the main food in the questionnaire and restrict the consumption of candy food and flour derivatives.
