He knows how to value people, they don't miss it, he defends their opinions.
"When a director hires you to classify the locker room and complete it with nice garments, you can't fuck and throw away everything there was and say, "It's like horror.""
"Find at least a couple of things you can weigh and recommend so that somebody can wear them," Mario says.
He himself also showed us that everything must fit into the so-called "placovka," i.e. the work bag.
It is fixed around the waist and you have all the necessary tools there.
They are objects such as scissors, like scissors scissors, peelings, or unmissables. There are also nylon thread (which serves the stylist during the stylist photo shoe shooters or hats), special hook clizers of garments in front, if it was larger (the pins and other types of hooks are not allowed, because they could damage the fabric), or a couture game.
